\n- Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp.\n- Norvane Utilities priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably. Its 2027 capex is up 12%.\n- Debt alone may not cover the largest spender, Pellham Power, whose 2027 capex is up 18%. The sources give nothing on Pellham's leverage, ratings or bond capacity, so that is a judgment rather than a finding.\n\n**Equity: weak.**\n- Pellham withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering because demand fell short.\n- Two other utility share offerings were cut back in size.\n- Pellham is now cutting 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and deferring two substation programmes until financing improves.\n\n**What it means:**\n- Utilities with debt headroom, like Norvane, look able to fund their plans.\n- Plans that depend on new equity, like Pellham's, will probably be scaled back or deferred.\n- For grid-equipment demand, the main risk is Pellham's roughly 40% cut to 2027 transformer orders. Pellham is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria.\n\n**Gaps:** The evidence covers one bond deal, one withdrawn equity deal and one quarter of spread data. I found no data on equity issuance sizes, valuations, or Norvane's leverage headroom.","ttft_ms":2558,"type":"result","duration_ms":36519,"uuid":"bd22aca6-b7f7-4e2f-b04a-eb54799984fe","ttft_stream_ms":1390,"time_to_request_ms":186,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":11,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":9,"input_attachments":39,"input_hooks":6,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":15,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":42,"init_frame_send":8,"engine_pickup":4,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":7,"request_announcements":18,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":4,"request_build":6},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":66,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":98,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":174,"process_an